r of the South Korean girl group Dal Shabet.","title":"Viki (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viki_%28singer%29"}},"Q18531271":{"id":"Q18531271","name":"Seo Ji-soo","ko":"서지수","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1994-02-11","death":"","birthplace":"Incheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2014","agencies":[{"name":"Woollim Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q50596","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q18437003","name":"Lovelyz","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jeezepizza/","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCYCe4xWgCypqAQWzPH5gZeA","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/a6bfccd5-dae7-4902-9055-528ccaf03806"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q26262599":{"id":"Q26262599","name":"Jennie","ko":"제니 김","birthName":"Kim Jennie","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Jennie Ruby Jane","Jennie Kim","Kim Jennie"],"birth":"1996-01-16","death":"","birthplace":"Seongnam","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"Odd Atelier","korean":true,"id":"Q124047821","start":"2024","end":""},{"name":"Columbia Records","korean":false,"id":"Q183387","start":"2024","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q25056945","name":"Blackpink","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"website":"https://www.jenn.ie/","instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jennierubyjane/","x":"https://x.com/jennierubyjane","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCNYi_zGmR519r5gYdOKLTjQ","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@jennierubyjane","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/250b0Wlc5Vk0CoUsaCY84M","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/779351de-0da5-4943-928b-495a3c40e8c0"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Jennie Kim is a South Korean singer, rapper, songwriter, and actress. Born in South Korea, she moved to New Zealand in 2004 and returned to South Korea to successfully audition for YG Entertainment in 2010. She rose to prominence as a member of the South Korean girl group Blackpink, which debuted in August 2016 and became one of the best-selling girl groups of all time. In November 2018, Jennie released her debut single \"Solo\", which topped South Korea's Circle Digital Chart and the US Billboard World Digital Songs chart; its music video was the first by a Korean female soloist to surpass one billion views on YouTube.","title":"Jennie (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jennie_%28singer%29"}},"Q26710983":{"id":"Q26710983","name":"Choi Yoo-jung","ko":"최유정","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Yoojung","Choi Yoojung","Choi Yu-jeong","Choi Yujeong"],"birth":"1999-11-12","death":"","birthplace":"Guri","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q32860762","name":"Weki Meki","start":"2017","end":"2024"},{"id":"Q54859942","name":"WJMK","start":"2018","end":"2024"},{"id":"Q23688122","name":"I.O.I","start":"2026","end":"2017"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/dbeoddl__/","x":"https://x.com/cyoojung_offcl","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC0syKfBsFrWg9rBfFxHZGaw","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@wm_choiyoojung","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1ygbGmBWGTX0llbLrD9648","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/edbdd442-74f7-4630-9097-5a73a3824a4c"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Choi Yoo-jung, known mononymously as Yoojung, is a South Korean singer and actress signed under Fantagio. She debuted as a member of I.O.I in May 2016 after achieving third place in the 2016 survival program Produce 101. In January 2017, I.O.I officially disbanded after eleven months of promotion. I.O.I briefly returned for a 10 year comeback in 2026. Following disbandment, she returned to her respective agency and eventually debuted with Weki Meki in August 2017. Choi debuted as a solo artist with the single album Sunflower in September 2022.","title":"Choi Yoo-jung (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Choi_Yoo-jung_%28singer%29"}},"Q43088647":{"id":"Q43088647","name":"Tag","ko":"TAG (가수)","birthName":"손영택","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Son Young-taek","Youngtaek"],"birth":"1998-04-13","death":"","birthplace":"Wansan-gu","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[{"name":"Woollim Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q50596","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q30007238","name":"Golden Child","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/son_yt7/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/db30f2fc-f4cb-48d3-a1bf-fd2cbbbc2767"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c0/%EA%B3%A8%EB%93%A0_%EC%B0%A8%EC%9D%BC%EB%93%9C_%28Golden_Child%29_%40_181123_KBS_MUSIC_BANK_45s.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EA%B3%A8%EB%93%A0_%EC%B0%A8%EC%9D%BC%EB%93%9C_(Golden_Child)_@_181123_KBS_MUSIC_BANK_45s.jpg","author":"NINE STARS","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":null},"Q4726727":{"id":"Q4726727","name":"Alina Smith","ko":"알리나 스미스","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1987-08-25","death":"","birthplace":"Saint Petersburg","nationality":["United States"],"height":null,"occupations":["record producer","songwriter","pianist","singer","musician"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[],"links":{"musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/5ed45b2e-3645-4c66-a73f-a69d3a2ff4b4"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Alina Smith is a Russian-American pop singer, songwriter and, record producer. She is a co-founder of the music writing and production company Lyre, and she has written and produced songs for artists including Betty Who, Itzy, Kep1er, Gabi DeMartino and Red Velvet.","title":"Alina Smith","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alina_Smith"}},"Q47524999":{"id":"Q47524999","name":"JooE","ko":"주이","birthName":"Lee Joo-won","birthNameEn":"Lee Joo-won","aliases":["Lee Joo-won"],"birth":"1999-08-18","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","rapper","dancer"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"Oneul Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q141572396","start":"2024","end":""},{"name":"MLD Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q61091637","start":"2016","end":"2023"}],"groups":[{"id":"Q27820706","name":"Momoland","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/j_oo.e_0en/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/a0daec29-e194-47b0-b252-eec5e3b0cf09"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Joo-won better known by her stage name JooE (주이), is a South Korean singer and rapper. She is a member of the girl group Momoland under former MLD Entertainment and current Inyeon Entertainment.","title":"JooE","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JooE"}},"Q483527":{"id":"Q483527","name":"Kim Jong-kook","ko":"김종국","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Jong-kuk","Kim Jong-guk"],"birth":"1976-04-25","death":"","birthplace":"Hapcheon County","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","television actor"],"debut":"1995","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q7853796","name":"Turbo","start":"","end":""},{"id":"Q20010782","name":"Running Man Brothers","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/kjk76/","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCoe-0EVDJnjlSoPK8ygcGwQ","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/60YNqzrSj7rJkuqHkpHPqG","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/f6a68f94-384c-47a2-85a8-81731e0a559c"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Jong-kook is a South Korean singer, entertainer, and actor. Kim debuted as a member of South Korean duo Turbo in 1995. The duo was considered to be one of the most popular idols in that time and sold out millions of albums in South Korea and Asia. Following the disbanding of the duo in 2000, Kim released his debut solo album, Renaissance, in December 2001. As a solo artist, Kim has received several awards, including three Golden Disc Awards, two Seoul Music Awards, two KBS Music Awards, two SBS Music Awards, two MBC Music Awards, one MBC Best 10 Music Award, one Mnet Asian Music Award, and one Melon Music Award.","title":"Kim Jong-kook","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Jong-kook"}},"Q485511":{"id":"Q485511","name":"Kwon So-hyun","ko":"권소현","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kwon So Hyun","Kwon Sohyun","Kwon So-hyeon","Kwon Sohyeon","Kwon So Hyeon"],"birth":"1994-08-30","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","model","actor"],"debut":"2009","agencies":[{"name":"Cube Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q484449","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q39682","name":"4Minute","start":"2009","end":"2016"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/kkwonsso_94/","x":"https://x.com/4M_kkwonsso","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/064eabba-43e2-41dd-aeb0-e6a7b177aa78"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kwon So-hyun, also known by the stage name Sohyun, is a South Korean actress and singer. She debuted as a member of the girl group Orange in 2005 and later became a member of 4Minute, which debuted under Cube Entertainment in 2009. In June 2016, 4Minute disbanded, and Kwon, along with fellow members Nam Ji-hyun, Heo Ga-yoon, and Jeon Ji-yoon, left Cube Entertainment after their contracts expired on June 14. She rejoined Cube Entertainment in September 2025 to pursue her acting career.","title":"Kwon So-hyun","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kwon_So-hyun"}},"Q497735":{"id":"Q497735","name":"Baek A-yeon","ko":"백아연","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Baek Ayeon","Baek A Yeon","Baek Ah-yeon","Baek Ah Yeon","Baek Ahyeon","Baek Ayun","Baek A-yun","Baek A Yun"],"birth":"1993-03-11","death":"","birthplace":"Seongnam","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","pianist","model"],"debut":"2012","agencies":[{"name":"JYP Entertainment","korean":true,"id"